IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`
IMPORT `ccc6-bestiality`
IMPORT `ccc6-tests-support`

-- Tests for s 160. Expected values decided from the text before each run.
-- The summary-conviction limbs that state no penalty take the penalty of s 787(1) as an input: here a stand-in value, "a fine in the discretion of the court" with six months, is passed in and must come back with the mode on summary conviction.

`s 160 test s 787(1) penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine in the discretion of the court`, `no fine is stated`
`s 160 test summary penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine in the discretion of the court`, `no fine is stated`

§ `s 160(7) bestiality means any contact, for a sexual purpose, with an animal`
#ASSERT `s 160(7) bestiality` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(7) bestiality` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- contact not for a sexual purpose: outside the text's "means"
#ASSERT `s 160(7) bestiality` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no contact with an animal

§ `s 160(1) Bestiality`
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the conduct is the offence of bestiality` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the conduct is the offence of bestiality` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the conduct is the offence of bestiality` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 10) `no imprisonment is stated`   -- "not exceeding ten years"
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 160 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 160 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 160(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`

§ `s 160(2) Compelling the commission of bestiality`
-- (compelled, the answer of s 160(7) bestiality)
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the conduct is the offence of compelling the commission of bestiality` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the conduct is the offence of compelling the commission of bestiality` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the conduct is the offence of compelling the commission of bestiality` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the conduct is the offence of compelling the commission of bestiality` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 10) `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 160 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 160 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 160(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`

§ `s 160(3) Bestiality in presence of or by child`
-- (what the person did, the age in years of the person in whose presence or who was incited, the answer of s 160(7) bestiality)
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` `s 160(3) committed bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years` 15 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` `s 160(3) incited a person under the age of 16 years to commit bestiality` 15.99 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` `s 160(3) committed bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years` 16 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- 16: not "under the age of 16 years"
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` `s 160(3) neither` 10 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the conduct is the offence of bestiality in the presence of, or by inciting, a person under 16` `s 160(3) committed bestiality in the presence of a person under the age of 16 years` 10 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no bestiality as defined in (7)
#ASSERT `s 160(3)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 14) (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 1)
#ASSERT `s 160(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test a summary punishment` `ss 150 to 182 test a term of two years less a day` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of months` 6)   -- minimum six months
#ASSERT `s 160(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`

§ `s 160(3.1) Representation of bestiality`
-- (knowingly, what the person did, it is such a representation)
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) publishes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) distributes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) transmits` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) sells` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) makes available` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) advertises` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` FALSE `s 160(3.1) publishes` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not knowingly
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) none of those` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(3.1) the conduct is the offence of publishing or distributing a representation of bestiality` TRUE `s 160(3.1) publishes` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a representation
-- (3.2) public good; (3.3) law and fact, motives
#ASSERT `s 160(3.2) section 160 gives a defence of public good against a charge under subsection (3.1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.2) section 160 gives a defence of public good against a charge under subsection (3.1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- extended beyond what served the public good
#ASSERT `s 160(3.2) section 160 gives a defence of public good against a charge under subsection (3.1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(a) the question is a question of law` `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct served the public good` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(a) the question is a question of law` `s 160(3.3) whether there is evidence that the conduct alleged went beyond what served the public good` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(a) the question is a question of law` `s 160(3.3) whether the conduct did or did not extend beyond what served the public good` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "a question of fact"
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(a) the question is a question of law` `s 160(3.3) another question` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(b) the motives of the accused are relevant` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "irrelevant"
#ASSERT `s 160(3.3)(b) the motives of the accused are relevant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(3.4)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` (`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` 5) `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 160(3.4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 160 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 160 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 160(3.4) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ss 150 to 182 test both`

§ `s 160(4) Order of prohibition or restitution`
-- (a): (sentenced under (1), (2), (3) or (3.4); what the order prohibits)
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` TRUE `s 160(4)(a) owning an animal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` TRUE `s 160(4)(a) having the custody or control of an animal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` TRUE `s 160(4)(a) residing in the same premises as an animal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` FALSE `s 160(4)(a) owning an animal` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not sentenced under any of those subsections
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused` TRUE `s 160(4)(a) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the shortest period of the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST `five years`   -- second or subsequent offence
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(a) the shortest period of the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- first offence: no minimum stated
-- (b): (sentenced under (1), (2), (3) or (3.4); the Attorney General applied or own motion; costs incurred by a carer; costs readily ascertainable)
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if the costs are readily ascertainable" fails: a power's gate (11-12 limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `... TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; no application and not on the court's own motion: an "on application" gate of the upon kind, which the sweep lists and answers as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05), limb by limb
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no one took care of an animal
#ASSERT `s 160(4)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of the animal's care` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 160(5) Breach of order`
#ASSERT `s 160(5) the conduct is the offence of contravening an order made under paragraph (4)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(5) the conduct is the offence of contravening an order made under paragraph (4)(a)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 160(5) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 160 test s 787(1) penalty` EQUALS `s 160 test summary penalty`
#ASSERT `s 160(5) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 160(6) Application`
#ASSERT `s 160(6) sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 160(6) sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order under paragraph (4)(a): the subsection is silent
